## Consumer findings during execution

The first installed matrix run fails four named-fixture ConjunctiveGraph cases (747 pass before maxfail stops), proving inherited routing alone did not preserve default-union selection. The writer owns the existing dataset-selection repair and attributable requalification. `_DatasetGraph` also shares the whole native store but carries `_graph_name`; its actual query scope needs coverage.

Executed a read-only genuine rdflib 7.6.0 scope probe using `/home/paudley/Active/purrdf/bindings/python/.venv/bin/python`, exit 0. Inputs: default graph `(ex:a,ex:p,ex:d)`, named g and h each `(ex:a,ex:p,ex:n)`. Dataset(false) plain BGP returns d; named view and processor(named view) plain BGP return n. Dataset `GRAPH ex:h` returns n, while named view and processor(named view) `GRAPH ex:h` both raise the genuine single-graph/dataset-required error. After assigning `dataset.default_union=True`, plain BGP returns d and n once, including default triples and deduplicating identical triples across named graphs. Exact probe queries are `SELECT ?o WHERE {?s <http://example.org/p> ?o}` and `SELECT ?o WHERE {GRAPH <http://example.org/h> {?s <http://example.org/p> ?o}}`. These oracle observations were sent to the writer. They are not candidate passes.

Duplicate-label lookup repair now reads last-occurrence indices. Sent the remaining actual last-unbound inconsistency: original asdict filters cells before duplicate overwrite, retaining a prior bound value when the final same-name occurrence is None. Genuine RDFLib asdict omits the label. Its get also returns None for an existing unbound label even when a default was supplied, using that default only for missing labels. Requested coherent final-label asdict/get repair and new-file controls. No upstream implementation was copied; source inspection establishes behavior only.

The writer's initial graph-scope repair adds a pre-execution traversal rejecting any GRAPH in a single-graph plan. This is a confirmed semantic blocker, not merely a possible risk: genuine rdflib 7.6.0 on an empty Graph returns [] for `SELECT ?s WHERE { ?s <http://example.org/p> ?o OPTIONAL { GRAPH <http://example.org/g> {?x ?p ?y} } }` and for the analogous `FILTER EXISTS { GRAPH ... }`; it raises the dataset-required error for the corresponding MINUS because its RHS is evaluated eagerly. Read-only oracle probe exit 0, exact version asserted. The eager presence scan rejects all three, changing the first two answers. Sent the writer the actual witnesses and required evaluation-time error semantics, preserving ordinary native work. Final repair and executed attribution remain pending.

Additional genuine oracle probe, exit 0: `SELECT ?x WHERE { BIND(IF(true,1,EXISTS { GRAPH <http://example.org/g> {?s ?p ?o}}) AS ?x) }` yields 1; replacing true with false raises dataset-required. These confirm lazy expression behavior independently of empty-driver behavior.

Source-level repair now removes the eager scan. The contextual compiler specializes `SINGLE_GRAPH` statically and wraps Graph nodes in the existing Apply with a boxed `dataset_required` policy leaf. Both existing outlined Apply entries reject only when actually reached. Validation constrains this marker to an empty driver/Graph RHS with no competing policy modes; clone, expression rebuild and property-function transforms preserve it. No second evaluation/parser home, ordinary EvalCtx/options field or dispatcher branch was added. New source and executed receipts must rebind the affected proof; this paragraph records inspected repair intent, not final runtime PASS.

## Full gate uncovered nested outermost binding defect

The final-frozen module receipt identifies native artifact SHA-256 `c08110b6c4f888380a088f1270ab602bf2b56cd6ac58e1874a8c27fc7026e7ee`, genuine oracle 7.6.0 and locked dependency SHA `06275d43821c8351f89f88071af043ce4c4645fe3adcf2126b2f28f031cafc01`. Independently checked the frozen Rust end manifest against current source, exit 0 at that sampling. The complete new file then passed 809 intermediate tests, but the actual full gate fails the untouched vendor `nested_filter_outermost_binding_propagation`: outer 4725 pass/4 strict xfail/1 skip/1 fail, vendor 80 pass/5 xfail/1 fail with no XPASS or stale key. This is a required repair, not permission to add a ledger entry. All earlier frozen contextual receipts need affected requalification after the compiler repair.

Independent reduced diagnostic executed against that installed module and genuine oracle, exit 0. Own query:

```sparql
PREFIX ex:<http://example.org/>
SELECT ?new WHERE {
  VALUES (?action ?old ?new ?t1) {
    (ex:a ex:old ex:good ex:t1) (ex:a ex:old ex:bad ex:t1)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?action ex:used ?t2 . ?old ex:member ?t2 .
    FILTER (?t1 != ?t2)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?new ex:member ?t2 }
  }
} ORDER BY ?new
```

Seven triples: a used t1,t2; old member t1,t2; good member t1,t2; bad member t1. Genuine oracle selects good only, candidate selects bad and good. A simpler middle VALUES version passed both; this narrows the missing inherited correlation to the real middle BGP/nonlazy-Join context rather than every nested EXISTS. Sent the small original witness and negative/control requirements to the writer. It copies no upstream implementation or test body.

Read actual compiler `expression`, `lookup`, `thaw`, leaf merge, Filter/Join build and source-fact collection, plus genuine FrozenBindings/context operations as behavioral evidence. In particular the oracle forget operation retains its full matched solution context separately from its filtered mapping; thaw of an empty mapping uses that context, not necessarily the operator input C. This distinction and explicit private context transport must be traced before any repair is accepted. Blindly filling every absent key of a nonempty mapping would contradict existing projected-empty/mapping-domain laws. Final source/real vendor and regression results remain pending.

Two attempted contextual carry repairs fail the same narrow native regression (2 rows versus 1; the prior 14 controls including 241-case matrix pass). The writer preserved both failures. The expression context-union and expanded private Project lists do not establish causal closure. Actual runtime Apply invokes substitution with DECLARED/PRESERVE=true, skipping the ordinary Project narrowing in that window; Apply's outer substitution masks declared inputs and then reconstructs them from bound driver cells. These inspected masks explain why a Project declaration alone is insufficient, but are not the observed cause of this witness.

Independent actual-plan diagnosis now identifies the cause. In `raw/t2-nested-context-plan-diagnostic.log`, C aliases for s,x,y,z are slots0,1,2,3. The middle `FILTER(x != y)` is emitted with x lookup `If(Bound(C_x), UNDEF, R_x)`; outer EXISTS has bound C_x, so this inner isolated Filter drops every middle witness before reaching nested EXISTS. The compiler marks only the top Filter at an EXISTS root as nonisolated, whereas its parser represents two leading Filter nodes for the two source conditions.

Executed genuine 7.6.0 translation metadata probe, exit 0, on `SELECT ?s WHERE { ?s ex:q ?z . ?s ex:p ?x FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s ex:p ?y FILTER(?x != ?y) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?z ex:r ?y } } }`: the executable outer EXISTS body is ONE Filter, `no_isolated_scope=True`, operand Join, expression ConditionalAndExpression containing both the relational condition and nested NOT EXISTS. This confirms the isolation mismatch directly. Sent the actual observation to the writer and parent, requiring preservation of group boundaries and combined-expression order/error/callback laws rather than another guessed carry fix. No new native substitution behavior is authorized or needed by this diagnosis. Final repaired source/regression/vendor evidence remains required.

Additional genuine multiple-filter probes, exit 0, expose the required operational continuation law: `SELECT ?x WHERE { VALUES ?x {1} FILTER(1/0) FILTER(EXISTS {GRAPH <http://example.org/g> {?s ?p ?o}}) }` raises dataset-required. Replacing first expression with false also raises; reversing EXISTS and false also raises. Genuine translated root expression is ConditionalAndExpression in source condition order. Its raw operand retrieval is eager before EBV conjunction, so distinct sequential Filter stages cannot suppress a later operational failure after an earlier false/error. Sent these actual witnesses to the writer. A leading-isolation-only patch would not discharge this consumer law; a compiler-only lowering can reuse existing expression/row continuation homes and must preserve ordinary native VM work.

## Coherent same-group repair inspected

The actual repair now folds only each contextual parser GroupState's collected filters into Expression::and before group_join can normalize away empty group ownership. Element::Filter appends in source order; Expression::and extends its left chain in that order. The shared VM compile.rs lines 484–494 emits each operand and its EBV before the final Kleene combination; its work-list transfer at lines 313–319 restores that evaluation order. Thus false/error operands do not prevent a later reached operational GRAPH refusal, while IF still uses its separate lazy branch implementation. OPTIONAL consumes the repaired owning group filter_count of one; nested child-group filters are not peeled into the owning group condition. Ordinary RDFLIB=false retains the old vector and wrapper loop, subject to final emitted-native proof.

