## Remaining observed local-projection defect

Read the completed historical raw/t2-group-filter-consumer-controls.log without executing Python: 817 pass and TWO real failures. The local-subselect/nested EXISTS witness from the earlier independent oracle probes selects both a and b instead of a; its negated variant selects nothing instead of b. The user narrowing Python validation does not erase a known source defect. Both variants require Rust-owned reproduction and repair; the writer and parent were notified.

Source hypothesis (not yet actual runtime diagnosis): Project correctly publishes only local names into its logical Mapping. At a nonisolated EXISTS root Filter, expression/map_exists_bodies builds its inner driver only from that immediate Mapping. With local bound, thaw's present marker is true, so an absent outer name receives UNDEF rather than inherited C_outer; the inner EXISTS is then uncorrelated. This is a different seam from the repaired syntactic filter ownership defect. Expanding public/logical projection domains or globally restoring every absent mapping name would be unsound; inherited expression context must preserve isolated-filter forgetting and explicit Project/mapping-domain laws. Final actual native regression and cause closure remain required.

